{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha_over_4pi_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha_over_4pi_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L344-L347","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.brane_tower_finite_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.brane_tower_finite_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L338-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.chirality_factor_class_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.chirality_factor_class_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L327-L336","doc":"**`ChiralityFactorClass` is consistent** — some `a_K` satisfies the\n`O(h²)` bound. This is *all* that is unconditionally available, and\nit is not a derivation of the chirality factor: the witness is the\nfirst-order polynomial itself. An instance at the actual Kauffman\nribbon-twist evaluation is the open work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alphaOver4PiInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alphaOver4PiInstance","kind":"instance","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L294-L304","doc":"**α/(4π) class — unconditional instance.**\n...\n    The existential `∃ z, z = α/(4π)` is closed by `rfl`. The\n    substantive open content — that the coefficient `1/(4π)` arises\n    as a multivariate polylogarithm regulator on a higher Bloch\n    group `B_n(ℂ)` (Goncharov 1995 / Borel 1974) — remains\n    upstream and is not addressed by this formal closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.zHabiroConvergenceInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.zHabiroConvergenceInstance","kind":"instance","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L276-L292","doc":"**z-Habiro convergence class — unconditional instance.**\n...\n    Take `M = 1`. Then `M > 0` (by `one_pos`) and `M < 1.11 = brane_tower_pole`\n    (by `norm_num`). This formal closure of the existential demand\n    does *not* close the upstream regularisation conjecture\n    `conj:brane-tower-z-habiro`: the substantive open content is\n    that the regularised brane-tower sum *evaluates* to a uniform\n    bound across the Yekutieli / q-Habiro truncation choices, not\n    merely that *some* `M < q_0` exists. The instance below\n    formally satisfies the §3b-cond hook; the structural claim\n    remains in the upstream block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha_over_4pi_structural","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha_over_4pi_structural","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L235-L242","doc":"**α/(4π) conditional theorem (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.AlphaOver4PiClass.higher_bloch_realised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.AlphaOver4PiClass.higher_bloch_realised","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L231-L231","doc":"The next-order coefficient is realised as a higher\nBloch-group regulator output, not a fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.AlphaOver4PiClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.AlphaOver4PiClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L228-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.AlphaOver4PiClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.AlphaOver4PiClass","kind":"class","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L221-L233","doc":"**α/(4π) higher Bloch group class.** A concrete instance asserts\nthat the next-order coefficient `1/(4π)` arises from a multi-\nvariate polylogarithm regulator on a higher Bloch group\n`B_n(ℂ)` for some `n ≥ 3` (Goncharov 1995 conjectures cover\nthe relevant uniqueness up to scalar). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha_over_4pi_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha_over_4pi_target","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L214-L219","doc":"The next-order self-energy correction to `1/α_EM` after the\n`2/(3π)` Bring zero-mode: empirically `≈ α/(4π) ≈ 5.81×10⁻⁴`,\nbringing the residual to `+5.7×10⁻⁸` (within CODATA error). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.brane_tower_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.brane_tower_finite","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L203-L209","doc":"**z-Habiro conditional theorem (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ZHabiroConvergenceClass.uniform_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ZHabiroConvergenceClass.uniform_bound","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L198-L198","doc":"The regularised brane-tower sum is finite for every\nisotope-relevant input, uniformly bounded by `M < q_0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ZHabiroConvergenceClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ZHabiroConvergenceClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L195-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ZHabiroConvergenceClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ZHabiroConvergenceClass","kind":"class","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L189-L201","doc":"**z-Habiro convergence class.** A concrete instance asserts the\nexistence of a uniform bound on the q-Habiro completion of\n`∑ Φ_q(z_i)` along the deformation `|V_i| → 1`. The bound is\nindependent of which Yekutieli finite-slice or q-Habiro\ntruncation is taken. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.brane_tower_pole","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.brane_tower_pole","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L182-L187","doc":"The brane-tower per-generator volume `z_i = |V_i|` for low\nisotopes lies near the first pole of `Φ_q` at `z = q_0 ≈ 1.11`,\nmaking each summand enormous and the analytic series divergent.\nA uniform z-Habiro bound regulates this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.kauffman_eval_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.kauffman_eval_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L156-L177","doc":"**The untwisted evaluation is `1`** — a consequence of the `O(h²)`\nbound, not an assumption.\n\nAt `h = 0` the first-order factor is `1` and the error budget\n`C · h²` is exactly `0`, so the bound pins `a_K 0 w ⟨c⟩` on the\nnose. This composes the class field with the definition of\n`chirality_factor_first_order`; neither states it alone, and the\nprevious encoding could not state it at all (its `a_K` was\nexistentially quantified, so there was no fixed function to\nevaluate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ChiralityFactorClass.kauffman_derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ChiralityFactorClass.kauffman_derivation","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L149-L149","doc":"Structural derivation of the chiral-case first-order factor from\nthe Kauffman framing formula on the Hecke ribbon category, with\nexplicit average-content factor: the ribbon-twist evaluation\n`a_K` agrees with `1 + w · ⟨c⟩ · h` to `O(h²)` near `h = 0`.\n\n**Two things changed on 2026-08-29, and both were load-bearing.**\n\n`a_K` is now a **parameter**, not an existential. It was\n`∃ a_K error_term, …`, which asserts only that *some* pair of\nfunctions differs by *something* times `h²` — satisfied by taking\n`a_K` to be the first-order polynomial itself and the error\nidentically zero, which is how the instance below discharged it.\nAn existential over the very object the claim is about says\nnothing about the Kauffman evaluation; a parameter does.\n\nThe error is now **bounded**, which is what `O(h²)` means. The\nold field wrote `+ error_term · h²` with `error_term` free, so\nthe `h²` was decoration: an unbounded coefficient times `h²` can\nbe any function at all.\n\nSame defect family as `HasQPlancherelCLT` (fixed in the same PR)\nand as the q-RH `hasse-weil-bound` axioms — *an external theorem\nasserted over a structure that does not carry the theorem's\nhypotheses*. Recorded in\n`docs/audits/2026-08-29-q-ns-conditional-class-audit.md`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ChiralityFactorClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ChiralityFactorClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ChiralityFactorClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.ChiralityFactorClass","kind":"class","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L114-L154","doc":"**Chirality factor class — strengthened.** A concrete instance\nasserts the Kauffman-framing-formula derivation of\n`a_K(β) = 1 + w(β) · ⟨c⟩_β · h + O(h²)` on the Hecke ribbon\ncategory `H_n(R, q)`, with the *specific* `⟨c⟩_β` value\ndetermined by the Wedderburn-weighted character average. The\n\"paper-empirical ansatz\" of the trivial case `⟨c⟩ = 1` is one\ninhabited instance; the structural content is in the\ncharacter-weighted average computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.chirality_factor_first_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.chirality_factor_first_order","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L98-L112","doc":"Carrier for the chirality factor at first order in\n`h = q - q⁻¹`. The Kauffman ribbon-twist derivation in\n`prop:chirality-writhe-ribbon-derivation` §Derivation actually\nyields `a_K(β) = 1 + w(β) · ⟨c⟩_β · h + O(h²)`, where\n`⟨c⟩_β` is the *braid-character-weighted average content*\n\n  ⟨c⟩_β  :=  Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(β) c(λ)  /  Σ_λ w_λ χ^λ(β)\n\n(Wedderburn-weighted, see §\"Substituting into a_K\").\nThe simplified ansatz `1 + w·h` is the special case\n`⟨c⟩_β = 1`, which holds only for specific braids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.term7_structural_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.term7_structural_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L91-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.term7ShellCorrectionInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.term7ShellCorrectionInstance","kind":"instance","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L74-L89","doc":"**Term 7 — unconditional instance (sign witness only).**\n\nWith the placeholder `alpha5_value = -1`, the existential is\nclosed: `α = -1 < 0` and `α = alpha5_value` by `rfl`. This\ninhabits the strengthened class with the SIGN constraint\ndischarged unconditionally; the substantive open content is\nthe *magnitude* derivation from the GS-filtration spectral\nsequence at ℓ=5. A future instance with the correct magnitude\nrequires the explicit structural derivation in\n`conj:shell-correction-term-seven`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.term7_structural","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.term7_structural","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L67-L72","doc":"**Term 7 conditional theorem (sorry-free).** Given the class,\nthe shell correction has the binding-enhancing sign and\nmatches the carrier value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.Term7ShellCorrectionClass.alpha5_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.Term7ShellCorrectionClass.alpha5_derived","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Structural existence of `α_5 < 0` as a categorical-derivation\noutput (binding-enhancing sign from shell-closure quorum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.Term7ShellCorrectionClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.Term7ShellCorrectionClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.Term7ShellCorrectionClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.Term7ShellCorrectionClass","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L53-L65","doc":"**Term-7 shell-correction class — strengthened.** A concrete\ninstance asserts (a) the existence of `α_5 < 0` as a real\noutput of the GS-filtration spectral sequence at level ℓ=5,\nand (b) that this `α_5` matches the structural carrier\n`alpha5_value`. The `α_5 < 0` constraint encodes the binding-\nenhancing structural argument from\n`shell-correction-term-seven.md` §\"Supporting (structural)\"\nitem 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha5_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OpenProblems.alpha5_value","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses.lean#L41-L51","doc":"Carrier for the Term-7 shell-correction coefficient `α_5`. The\nstructural form derived in `conj:shell-correction-term-seven`\nis `Term 7(T_w) = α_5 · χ_5(T_w)`, where `χ_5` is the\nlevel-5 character projector summing over height-6 partitions\nweighted by Wedderburn `w_λ = dim_q(λ)² / [n]_q!`. The sign\nconstraint `α_5 < 0` is binding-enhancing — confirmed\nempirically (helium-4 doubly magic excess) and structurally\n(level-5 = first shell-closure quorum). ","signatureChunk":0}]}